Cleaned epochs derivative
=========================

Generated from the raw BIDS dataset with make_cleaned_epochs.py (https://github.com/parasmemon/tcre-overt-covert-speech-eeg).

Processing steps (applied to the TCRE array channels of every participant):
1. Notch filter at 60 Hz.
2. Band-pass filter 1-40 Hz (MNE-Python 1.12.1, default zero-phase FIR).
3. Epochs from -0.5 to 2.5 s relative to each picture-onset marker (Stimulus/Overt, Stimulus/Covert).
4. Baseline correction using -0.5 to 0 s.
No channels or epochs were rejected. The original sampling rate is kept.

Channels: only the TCRE array channels are included. Odd-numbered channels are TCRE signals and even-numbered channels are the emulated disc signals of the same electrode.
The EOG channels (two standard disc electrodes placed above and to the right of one eye; channels 41-42 of sub-07, sub-08, sub-09, sub-14, sub-15 and sub-16, and channels 63-64
of sub-11, sub-12 and sub-13) are not included here; they are available, labelled as EOG, in the raw data.
Electrodes per array (F4/P6/F3/P5): 5/5/5/5 (40 channels), 7/7/7/7 (56), 8/8/8/8 (64), and 8/7/8/8 (62 channels;
sub-11, sub-12, sub-13, whose P6 array had seven electrodes).

Files: sub-XX/eeg/sub-XX_task-OvertCovert_desc-cleaned_epo.fif (MNE .fif format).
Load with:  epochs = mne.read_epochs("sub-01/eeg/sub-01_task-OvertCovert_desc-cleaned_epo.fif")

Channel and trial counts per participant are listed in qc_summary.tsv.
